{%- comment -%}
  Standalone reviews page — the homepage's "Read all 747 on memobrick.com"
  link already pointed at /pages/happy-customers before this template
  existed, so this fills a gap the site was already expecting.

  Reuses the same #revTrack/#revPrev/#revNext/#revMore markup and ids the
  homepage uses — memobrick.js's realReviews() and reviews-rail code both
  just do document.querySelector for these ids, so the same real review
  data (customer photos included) powers this page automatically with no
  new JS and no duplicated review array to keep in sync.

  Known limitation: the review grid itself is rendered by JavaScript from
  the REVIEWS array in memobrick.js, so it won't appear in view-source or
  to a crawler that doesn't execute JS. The h1/intro and the
  AggregateRating structured data below are server-rendered and always
  present regardless. Moving REVIEWS into a Liquid-readable data source
  (a metafield or JSON asset) would let the review grid itself be
  server-rendered too — flagged as a follow-up, not done here, since it
  changes how review data is maintained going forward.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Product",
  "name": "MemoBrick custom photo mosaic",
  "aggregateRating": {
    "@type": "AggregateRating",
    "ratingValue": "4.8",
    "reviewCount": "747"
  }
}
</script>

{%- render 'site-header' -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "MemoBrick", "item": {{ request.origin | append: '/' | json }} },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Happy customers", "item": {{ canonical_url | json }} }
  ]
}
</script>
<div class="wrap" style="padding:48px 20px 20px;max-width:1160px">
  <p style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3)">
    <a href="/" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none">MemoBrick</a> <span aria-hidden="true">›</span> Happy customers
  </p>
  <h1 style="font-family:var(--display);font-size:32px;letter-spacing:-.03em;margin:10px 0 8px">
    747 reviews. These are their photos.
  </h1>
  <p style="color:var(--ink-2);font-size:16px;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 34px">
    The proof before production, the hours spent building it together, and what happens when someone
    finally sees it. Every photo below was taken by the customer who wrote the review.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="wrap">
  <div class="revrail">
    <button class="revnav prev" id="revPrev" aria-label="Previous reviews">‹</button>
    <div class="rev-grid" id="revTrack"></div>
    <button class="revnav next" id="revNext" aria-label="More reviews">›</button>
  </div>
  <div class="revmore">
    <button class="mini" id="revMore">Show more reviews</button>
    <a class="mini" href="https://loox.io/s/4JeBfbNCQq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See the full feed on Loox</a>
  </div>
  <p style="text-align:center;margin:36px 0 70px">
    <a class="btn btn-red" href="/pages/editor">Start designing your MemoBrick</a>
  </p>
</div>

{%- render 'site-footer' -%}
